    "summary": "Acoustic gems and fiery electric set with standout Morning Dew",
    "blurb": "The July 11 1970 Fillmore East show opens with a rare acoustic set featuring Jerry’s pedal‑steel work and Pigpen’s organ solo despite laryngitis. The second set erupts into high‑energy rock, highlighted by a powerful Morning Dew. Overall the performance is strong, though the only available tape is a fair audience recording.",
    "review": "On July 11, 1970 at New York’s Fillmore East the Dead delivered an unusual two‑part experience. Set 1 was an acoustic showcase that began with gospel‑tinged numbers and included a heartfelt rendition of “So Sad (To Watch Good Love Go Bad)”, while Jerry Garcia slipped in pedal‑steel tones that some fans even suspect early wah‑wah use. Pigpen, battling laryngitis, still managed an inspiring organ solo that underscored the set’s intimacy. The electric Set 2 flipped the vibe, launching into a blistering “Morning Dew” and driving through classics like “Good Lovin’”, “China Cat Sunflower”→“I Know You Rider”, and “Uncle John’s Band”. Though the sole recording (gd70-07-11.aud.cotsman.9379.sbefail.shnf) is a fair, left‑channel‑only audience tape with noticeable hiss, it captures enough of the band’s energy to make this show worth a listen for fans interested in that unique acoustic/electric contrast.",
